				"README.md": {
					"diff": "--- published/README.md\n+++ rebuilt/README.md\n@@ -1,132 +1,56 @@\n-# Text Mask Core\n+# [![Text Mask](assets/logo.png)](https://github.com/text-mask/text-mask/#readme)\n \n-This module contains the core functions that power Text Mask. Currently, Text Mask\n-has a wrapper for React, which can be used directly.\n+⚠️ This library is not maintained. Pull-requests and issues are not monitored. Below are some alternatives to `text-mask` (**Please note** that the alternatives below are not checked or verified by the maintainers of Text Mask):\n \n-However, Text Mask Core functions could be useful on their own. That's why they are published\n-and documented here as a separate module.\n+* https://github.com/uNmAnNeR/imaskjs\n+* https://github.com/JsDaddy/ngx-mask\n+* https://github.com/Tinkoff/maskito\n+* https://github.com/mertohancan/react-text-mask-modern\n \n-## Getting started\n+If you know other alternatives that should be listed here, email me at msafi@msafi.com.\n \n-To download the script, use npm.\n+-----\n \n-```bash\n-npm i text-mask-core --save\n-```\n+[![Build Status](https://travis-ci.org/text-mask/text-mask.svg?branch=master)](https://travis-ci.org/text-mask/text-mask)\n \n-### Include it\n+Text Mask is an input mask library. It can create input masks for phone, date, currency, zip code, percentage, email, \n+and literally anything!\n \n-After installing with npm, you could possibly do something like this from your `index.html`:\n+There are convenient wrappers for React, Angular 2, Ember, and Vue.\n \n-```html\n-<script src=\"./node_modules/text-mask-core/dist/textMaskCore.js\"></script>\n-```\n+## Live demo\n \n-Including this file in your source code will expose the global object `textMaskCore`.\n+See it in action, [check out the demo page](https://text-mask.github.io/text-mask/).\n \n-Or if you're using Node.js or a bundler such as webpack or Browserify, you can require\n-`textMaskCore` as such:\n+## Installation and usage\n \n-```js\n-var textMaskCore = require('text-mask-core')\n-```\n+* [React](react#readme)\n+* [Angular 2](angular2#readme) or [Angular 1](angular1#readme)\n+* [Ember](ember#readme)\n+* [Vue](vue#readme)\n+* [Vanilla JS](vanilla#readme)\n \n-## How to use\n+## Expected to work with...\n \n-`textMaskCore` exposes three functions:\n+IE9+, Android, Samsung Internet, Windows Phone, iOS, Opera, Firefox, Safari, and Chrome\n \n-* conformToMask\n-* adjustCaretPosition\n-* convertMaskToPlaceholder\n+## Flexible\n \n-### Overview\n+Text Mask is very configurable and allows you to create any type of input mask with minimal APIs.\n+[See the documentation for details](https://github.com/text-mask/text-mask/blob/master/componentDocumentation.md#readme).\n \n-The general idea is to take user input, conform it to your desired mask using `conformToMask`,\n-and then apply the output of `conformToMask` to the value of the HTML input element.\n-Once you do that however, the caret position will be lost. You can then use `adjustCaretPosition`\n-to restore the caret to its proper position.\n+## Extendable\n \n-To learn more about how to do that, see the API documentation below:\n+You can easily expand the base functionality of Text Mask with addons for more mask types. \n+[Checkout existing addons](https://github.com/text-mask/text-mask/tree/master/addons/#readme).\n \n-## API documentation\n+## Robust\n \n-### `convertMaskToPlaceholder(mask)`\n+Text Mask supports pasting, browser auto-fill, and all operations that a user would expect while interacting with\n+an input field.\n \n-This function takes a mask (string), i.e. `11/11/1111`, and returns a placeholder (string).\n+It works on mobile, has no 3rd party dependencies, and has a tiny footprint (less than 4KB gzipped).\n \n-```js\n-const placeholder = convertMaskToPlaceholder('11/11/1111')\n+## For any questions, suggestions, or feature requests\n \n-placeholder // __/__/____\n-```\n-\n-You can use this function to initialize an `input` element to a placeholder value.\n-\n",
